# Culture-MAP V2 AI Coding Agent Rules

All AI agents (Copilot, Cursor, etc.) working on this project MUST follow the workflows and skills defined in the `.agent/` directory.

## 🛠 Required Workflows

1. **MCP Workflow** ([.agent/workflows/MCP.md](.agent/workflows/MCP.md)):
   - Before starting any task, perform deep analysis using Sequential Thinking.
   - Always verify SDK/library best practices using Context7 and Tavily.
   - Do NOT trust existing code patterns; verify against 2025/2026 documentation.

2. **Doc-Guided Optimization** ([.agent/skills/doc-guided-optimization/SKILL.md](.agent/skills/doc-guided-optimization/SKILL.md)):
   - Prioritize performance (React rendering, Liveblocks sync).
   - Use latest Gemini models (e.g., `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`).
   - Implement "Thinking" capabilities for complex reasoning.

3. **SDK Version Check** ([.agent/skills/sdk-version-check/SKILL.md](.agent/skills/sdk-version-check/SKILL.md)):
   - Verify if libraries are deprecated (e.g., use `@google/genai` instead of `@google/generative-ai`).

## 📋 Operational Rules

- Always break down tasks into an `implementation_plan.md`.
- Use `mcp_context7` for documentation queries before `mcp_tavily`.
- When modifying AI logic, ensure the `thinkingBudget` or `thinkingLevel` is correctly set based on the model version.
- Use atomic commits and task-based progress tracking.
